  "obligation": "Execute modern try_table, throw and throw_ref through the single VM, preserving original tag/reference identity, payload roots, trap classification and tail-frame handler lifetime.",
  "representation": "One WasmException cell owns original tag and payload. Four appended residual operations share VM heap and activation machinery. Static try regions lower to existing Handler records and catch trampolines; typed JsError transport derives the exception reference from its existing thrown slot. One handler-target operation serves initial and instruction errors, preserving JavaScript PC behavior. Traps and ordinary JavaScript errors bypass Wasm catches; null throw_ref is a typed trap. Complete constructor windows use shared validation/liveness and named layout.",
